{"name":"Apple Jack","hex":"#8b974e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common, firm, round fruit produced by a tree of the genus Malus.","The fruit of the tree Malus domestica, chiefly with a green, red, or yellow skin, cultivated in temperate climates for cidermaking, cooking, and eating. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (something) appear like an apple (noun sense 1.1).","To become like an apple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple"},{"term":"jack","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A coarse medieval coat of defence, especially one made of leather. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A man.","A policeman or detective;  a military policeman."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jack"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apple Jack","blocks":[{"text":"Apple Jack or The Legend of Apple Jack is a 2003 American short film directed by Mark Whiting, and produced by Tranquility Pictures. The filming was performed on Sable Ranch, Canyon Country, California."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/The_Legend_of_Apple_Jack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Jack","wikidata":"Q257798"},{"title":"Apple Jack (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Apple Jack is a puzzle-platform video game developed by British indie developer Tim Sycamore under the name My Owl Software. It was released on 29 May 2010 through Xbox Live for the Xbox 360."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Apple-jack-video-game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Jack_(video_game)","wikidata":"Q4781190"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/The_Legend_of_Apple_Jack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/da/The_Legend_of_Apple_Jack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Legend_of_Apple_Jack.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Apple-jack-video-game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Apple-jack-video-game.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AApple-jack-video-game.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/500px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/1280px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and